   "summary": "The law amended section 412 of title 3 to add a new subsection (c) allowing covered employees to substitute available paid leave for unpaid leave under section 102(a)(1)(A) or (B) of the Family and Medical Leave Act of 1993 [2020-116-283-412-3], and it added a new subsection (a)(3) exempting that leave from the 12-month and 1,250-hour eligibility requirement [2020-116-283-412-1]. It also redesignated former subsections (c) and (d) as subsections (d) and (e), and it made conforming changes to subsection (d), including adding a regulations clause in subsection (d)(2)(C) and updating subsection (e)(1) to refer to subsection (c) as in effect on the date of enactment of the Presidential and Executive Office Accountability Act [2020-116-283-412-2] [2020-116-283-412-4] [2020-116-283-412-5] [2020-116-283-412-6] [2020-116-283-412-7].",
